"""Additional mechanism-specific explanation and measurement evidence, written for each model."""
D={}
def d(key,mechanism,verify,failure): D[key]=dict(mechanism=mechanism,verify=verify,failure=failure)
d('brake','延遲項與速度成正比，減速項與速度平方成正比；把兩項分開後，才能選擇改善控制延遲或增加有效制動的方案。若存在坡度，應另加沿坡重力，不能只改總距離。~The delay term is linear in speed and the deceleration term is quadratic. Separating them reveals whether control latency or effective braking deserves attention. A gradient requires an added gravitational component, not an arbitrary adjustment to the final distance.',
'用獨立里程或地速核對輪速積分，報告濕乾軌差異及停車距離的重複試驗範圍。~Check integrated wheel speed against independent distance or ground speed, and report wet-dry differences and repeated stopping-distance ranges.',
'應比較壓力建立與地速下降先後，避免誤判煞車故障。~Compare pressure build-up with ground-speed decay before diagnosing a brake fault.')
d('cant','殘餘加速度的正負表示側向作用方向，而不是安全與危險的二元判斷。半徑、軌距與高差必須使用一致長度單位，車體感受還會受到懸吊轉角影響。~The sign of residual acceleration identifies its lateral direction, not a binary safe-unsafe outcome. Radius, gauge and rail-level difference require consistent length units. Carbody response is additionally affected by suspension rotation, which this geometric estimate does not resolve.',
'用實測半徑和高差重算平衡速度，保留感測器安裝角的校正值及量測不確定度。~Recalculate equilibrium speed from measured radius and cant, retaining mounting-angle corrections and uncertainty for the acceleration sensor.',
'需核對高差符號與曲線方向，防止左右軌互換。~Check cant sign against curve direction to prevent swapping the inner and outer rails.')
d('jerk','斜坡較緩時達到同一速度需要額外時間，且短站距可能沒有足夠時間維持最大加速度。控制器因此應以完整速度軌跡為輸出，而非只檢查單一加速度峰值。~A gentler ramp takes more time to reach a target speed, and short station spacing may leave no interval at peak acceleration. The controller therefore needs a complete speed trajectory rather than acceptance based only on one acceleration peak.',
'以已知時間基準檢查取樣間隔，並比較不同濾波頻寬對加加速度峰值的影響。~Verify sampling intervals against a known time reference and compare how alternative filter bandwidths change the estimated jerk peak.',
'需查看原始加速度，判別峰值是否由數值微分產生。~Inspect raw acceleration to determine whether a peak was created by numerical differentiation.')
d('capacity','此式計算的是通過指定斷面的名目服務率，不能表示月台能容納多少人。需求在空間或時間上集中時，某站可以過載，即使整條線的平均載客率仍低。~This expression estimates a nominal service rate across a specified section, not how many people a platform can hold. Concentrated demand can overload one station even when average occupancy across the complete line remains relatively low.',
'逐列核對上車、下車與留下人數的守恆，並以同一計數時間窗比較需求和服務量。~Check conservation of boarding, alighting and remaining passengers for every train, using identical counting windows for demand and delivered service.',
'應查驗未登車隊列，避免把滿載通過當成需求已服務。~Inspect passengers left behind instead of interpreting a full passing train as demand served.')
d('dwell','均分模型是檢查單位和量級的起點；真實發車須等最後必要門組完成。上車和下車方向互相干擾時，應用分階段或逐門事件模型重新識別流率。~Uniform allocation is a starting point for units and scale, while actual departure waits for the last required door group. If boarding and alighting interfere, use phased or door-by-door event models to identify the relevant exchange rates.',
'以影片事件時間和門控紀錄交叉對時，分別統計交換完成與發車確認的尾端分布。~Synchronise video event times with door-controller logs and separately report the tails of exchange completion and departure confirmation.',
'先核對門口人數，避免把旅客集中誤診為門機速度下降。~Check doorway demand before misdiagnosing passenger concentration as slower door machinery.')
d('turnback','只要有兩條路徑共享道岔或保護區，表面上分開的月台仍可能互相限制。時序模型應包含占用開始、列車清空和進路釋放三個不同時間，而非一個站停數字。~Platforms that appear separate can still constrain each other through shared points or protection zones. A sequence model needs distinct times for occupation, physical clearance and route release rather than representing all three by one station dwell value.',
'用占用指示與實際尾端清空時間互證，並列出各活動能否平行及其必要前置事件。~Cross-check occupation indication against actual rear-end clearance and list whether each task can overlap and which preceding events it requires.',
'若尾端尚未清空，不能以換端完成取代進路釋放證據。~Cab-change completion cannot substitute for route-release evidence while the train rear remains uncleared.')
d('regen','效率係數應涵蓋已宣告的轉換鏈；若把網路接受率也納入，必須說明觀測時間窗。只從速度差估計可回收量，不能辨認能量流向電網、電阻或輔助設備。~The efficiency must cover a declared conversion chain. If it includes network receptivity, the observation window must be stated. A speed change alone cannot identify how energy divides among the supply network, braking resistors and auxiliary equipment.',
'檢查功率計正負方向與積分時間邊界，以能量平衡殘差確認回送量未被重複計入。~Check meter polarity and integration boundaries, then use the energy-balance residual to confirm that exported energy has not been counted twice.',
'若回送受限，需查架線電壓及電阻制動記錄。~When export is curtailed, inspect line-voltage and resistor-braking records together.')
d('drag','阻力是速度平方關係，而牽引功率還要乘一次速度。把逆風納入時應使用相對空氣速度；滾動阻力與坡度功率是另外的能量途徑，不能被此氣動項取代。~Drag varies with squared speed, while traction power introduces another speed factor. Headwind requires relative air speed. Rolling resistance and gradient power are separate energy paths and cannot be replaced by this aerodynamic term.',
'同步紀錄風向風速與地速，將穩速段牽引功率扣除可辨識的坡度和輔助負載。~Record wind vector and ground speed together, then remove identifiable gradient and auxiliary loads from steady-running traction power.',
'需核對風向，避免把順風和逆風的相對速度互換。~Check wind direction to avoid reversing the relative-speed treatment of headwind and tailwind.')
d('tunnelwave','阻塞比是列車迎風面積除以隧道面積，不能用直徑比代替。此量級模型忽略洞口緩衝、泄壓孔與反射波；要預測波形或微壓波，還需非定常流動與邊界資料。~Blockage ratio is train frontal area divided by tunnel area, not a ratio of diameters. The scale model omits portal hoods, relief openings and reflected waves. Predicting waveforms or micro-pressure waves requires unsteady flow and boundary data.',
'在洞口與洞內配置同步壓力測點，對照列車頭部通過時刻，分辨首波與後續反射。~Synchronise pressure sensors at the portal and inside the tunnel with nose-passage time, distinguishing the first wave from later reflections.',
'單點峰值不足以判別首波，須檢查測點間傳遞時差。~A single peak cannot identify the first wave; inspect propagation delay between sensors.')
d('pantograph','線密度決定單位長度的慣性，張力提供恢復作用，因此波速平方與張力成正比。提高張力也改變支承受力；波速裕度只能作篩檢，不能推定接觸力必然均勻。~Linear density represents inertia per unit length and tension supplies restoring force, so squared wave speed scales with tension. Higher tension also changes support loading. A wave-speed margin is a screening measure, not proof of uniform contact force.',
'核對接觸線張力、單位長度質量及量測位置，並用接觸力和離線事件檢查動態品質。~Verify contact-wire tension, mass per unit length and measurement location, then examine contact force and loss-of-contact events for dynamic quality.',
'波速符合估算仍可能離線，需查看接觸力的時間歷程。~Agreement in wave-speed estimates does not rule out contact loss; inspect contact-force histories.')
d('thermal','溫差應相對於鋼軌實際無應力狀態，而非任意室溫。完全拘束估算給出軸向應力尺度；當扣件滑移或軌道彎曲出現時，需要位移相容和側向穩定分析。~Temperature change must reference the rail’s actual stress-free state, not an arbitrary room temperature. Full restraint gives an axial stress scale. Fastener slip or track curvature requires displacement compatibility and lateral stability analysis beyond this expression.',
'以鋼軌接觸式溫度計校驗遙測值，核對應變零點，並保留日夜循環的升降溫路徑。~Calibrate remote readings against a contact rail thermometer, verify strain zero, and retain heating and cooling paths across the daily cycle.',
'需查鎖定軌溫紀錄，不能以當天最低氣溫當無應力點。~Check stress-free-temperature records rather than using the day’s minimum air temperature as the reference.')
d('seismic','此處以相同距離比較兩種波速，屬簡化幾何模型。實際感測站可能不在線路與震源之間；可用時間還包括資料品質檢查及保護命令發送，不能只比較波速。~The exercise compares two wave speeds over the same distance and therefore uses simplified geometry. A real sensor may not lie between the source and railway. Available time also includes data-quality checks and protection-command delivery, not only wave propagation.',
'以完整訊號重播核對每個時間戳，將總延遲分解成判定、網路與列車端處理。~Use full-chain signal replay to verify every timestamp and separate total delay into decision, network and train-side processing components.',
'感測成功不等於制動成功，須查列車收到命令後的動作。~Successful detection is not successful braking; inspect the train response after command receipt.')
d('settlement','相同端點坡度可以對應完全不同的中間形狀，因此坡度不能單獨表示軌道曲率。測點間距必須小於欲辨認的變形尺度，並將高程誤差相對於基長傳遞到坡度結果。~Identical endpoint gradient can hide very different intermediate shapes, so gradient alone cannot describe track curvature. Survey spacing must resolve the deformation length scale, and elevation uncertainty must be propagated relative to the baseline into the reported gradient.',
'重複觀測同一測點並做閉合檢核，以另一穩定基準核對零點，報告高差與基長各自誤差。~Repeat identical points with closure checks, verify zero against another stable reference, and report separate errors for elevation difference and baseline.',
'高差異常需先查基點，不能立刻推定路基局部下沉。~An unusual level difference requires a datum check before inferring local earthwork settlement.')
d('bridge','跨長四次方使幾何誤差特別重要，但只有在相同支承、均布荷載及截面條件下才可比較。將毫米轉成公尺後再核對剛度，可避免把量測位移誤差變成材料性能判斷。~Fourth-power span dependence makes geometry important, but comparison requires the same support, uniform-load and section assumptions. Convert millimetres and metres consistently before checking stiffness, so a displacement-unit error does not become a false conclusion about material properties.',
'先以已知荷載校對位移計量程與零點，分別記錄載入卸載路徑及支點運動。~Check displacement-sensor range and zero under known loading, recording loading and unloading paths separately from support movement.',
'若卸載後仍有位移，須區分基座滑移與構件殘留變形。~Residual displacement after unloading requires distinguishing fixture slip from permanent structural deformation.')
d('suspension','固有頻率和振幅不是同一資訊，阻尼主要影響峰值和衰減。空車與滿載質量不同時，軌道某一波長可能落在不同激振頻率比，應同時考慮速度與載重。~Natural frequency and amplitude contain different information; damping primarily affects peaks and decay. Empty and loaded masses can place one track wavelength at different excitation-frequency ratios. Speed and loading therefore need to be considered together.',
'由自由衰減同時辨識頻率及衰減率，檢查感測器是否位於同一振型的有效位置。~Identify frequency and decay rate together from free decay, and verify that sensors occupy useful positions for the same vibration mode.',
'需量測衰減率，不能以峰值頻率不變排除阻尼故障。~Measure decay rate; an unchanged peak frequency cannot exclude a damping fault.')
d('wheelheat','有效受熱質量可以小於構件總質量，短時接觸表面的熱量也未必已傳到內部。能量平衡應先界定摩擦分配比例，再評估對流、輻射和間歇冷卻是否可忽略。~The effective heated mass can be smaller than total component mass, and short-duration surface heat may not reach the interior. First define frictional energy allocation, then assess whether convection, radiation and cooling between events can be neglected.',
'在不同深度保留溫度曲線並核對感測器反應時間，用初末能量平衡檢查平均溫升。~Retain temperature histories at different depths, verify sensor response time, and use initial-to-final energy balance to check mean temperature rise.',
'若表面與內部溫差很大，集中熱容量假設便不足。~A large surface-to-core temperature difference indicates that the lumped thermal-capacity assumption is insufficient.')
d('adhesion','法向荷重應只取實際驅動接觸點的總量，不能自動使用整列重量。此上限也不描述黏著峰後的滑移控制；若輪重轉移，就要以每個接觸點重新分配。~Normal load must include only the driven contacts, not automatically the weight of the whole train. This bound does not describe slip control beyond the adhesion peak. Wheel-load transfer requires a new allocation across individual contact points.',
'以獨立地速校對輪周速度，核實輪徑設定，再按乾濕條件與軸荷分類比對。~Calibrate wheel-periphery speed against independent ground speed, verify wheel-diameter settings, and compare results by wetness condition and axle load.',
'先查輪徑與地速誤差，避免把量測偏差當成真滑轉。~Check diameter and ground-speed errors before interpreting measurement bias as actual wheel slip.')
d('grade','坡度以升高量除以水平距離表示，百分比與小數不可混用。此項只表示重力位能增加的速率，總牽引功率還要加上加速、滾動、氣動及轉換損失。~Gradient is rise divided by horizontal distance, so percentage and decimal representations must not be mixed. This term only gives the rate of gravitational potential-energy increase. Total traction demand also includes acceleration, rolling resistance, aerodynamics and conversion losses.',
'由高程剖面核對坡度，使用同一時間窗比對速度與牽引功率，另列非重力負載。~Check gradient from the elevation profile, compare speed and traction power over one time window, and list non-gravitational loads separately.',
'功率不足時須分辨坡度阻力與黏著限制，不能只加大電流。~When power is insufficient, distinguish gradient resistance from adhesion limits rather than only increasing current.')
d('voltage','回路電阻必須包含饋電與回流路徑，還需說明是否納入接頭和變電站等效阻抗。電流固定是簡化；實際定功率負載在電壓降低時可能增加電流並擴大壓降。~Loop resistance must include supply and return paths, with joints and substation equivalent impedance explicitly included or excluded. Fixed current is a simplification: a constant-power load can draw more current as voltage falls and thereby increase the drop.',
'同步量測供電端與受電端電壓及回路電流，核對接線極性和設備接頭的額外壓降。~Measure supply voltage, receiving voltage and loop current synchronously, checking polarity and extra voltage drops across equipment connections.',
'需核對回流路徑，否則可能把接頭故障藏在錯估電阻中。~Verify the return path so a faulty connection is not hidden inside an incorrect resistance estimate.')
d('powerloss','此式是導體焦耳熱，並不是列車全部耗電。電阻會隨溫度改變，而並聯饋電使電流重新分配；比較兩方案時應保持相同功率交付邊界，避免只移轉損失位置。~The expression represents conductor Joule heat, not all train consumption. Resistance changes with temperature, and parallel feeding redistributes current. Compare schemes at the same delivered-power boundary to avoid reporting loss relocation as an actual reduction.',
'由電流時間歷程積分損失，量測導體溫度以校正電阻，並比對兩端功率差。~Integrate losses over the current history, measure conductor temperature to correct resistance, and compare with the difference between terminal powers.',
'尖峰電流不能用平均電流取代，否則平方項損失被低估。~Peak current cannot be replaced by mean current without understating losses from the squared term.')
d('isolation','此簡化歐姆模型描述絕緣路徑的漏電尺度，不能替代保護接地或接觸電壓評估。測試電壓、濕度與設備斷接狀態必須保留，否則不同量測結果無法比較。~This Ohmic approximation describes leakage through an insulation path, not protective earthing or touch-voltage performance. Test voltage, humidity and equipment isolation state must be recorded; otherwise readings from different tests cannot be meaningfully compared.',
'檢查儀器量程、測試電壓及斷接狀態，以同條件重複試驗分辨受潮與接線差異。~Verify meter range, test voltage and isolation state, then repeat under matching conditions to distinguish moisture effects from wiring differences.',
'不得把正常回流當漏電，需先確認量測邊界與接點。~Do not classify normal return current as leakage; first confirm measurement boundaries and connections.')
d('localize','定位誤差若源於輪徑比例偏差，會隨里程累積；隨機雜訊則可能有不同統計行為。保護邊界應使用與錯誤模型相符的包絡，不能用平均誤差掩蓋偏差。~A wheel-diameter scale error accumulates with distance, while random noise can follow a different statistical pattern. A protective boundary needs an envelope consistent with the error model rather than an average that hides persistent bias.',
'在已知參考點核對位置，將比例偏差與隨機殘差分開，檢查往返兩方向是否一致。~Check position at known references, separate scale bias from random residuals, and test consistency in both directions of travel.',
'若誤差隨距離單調增加，先查比例校正而非任意平滑。~If error grows monotonically with distance, inspect scale calibration before applying arbitrary smoothing.')
d('communication','傳輸時間不是訊息年齡的全部，排隊、重送及接收端處理也可能占主要比例。安全邏輯應明確定義逾時後的狀態；成功收到舊封包不能當成最新授權。~Transmission time is not the entire message age; queueing, retransmission and receiver processing may dominate. Safety logic needs an explicit state after timeout. Successful receipt of an old packet is not equivalent to a fresh movement authority.',
'以發送與接收端同步時鐘核對端到端延遲，記錄重送次數、封包遺失及最長連續中斷。~Use synchronised sender and receiver clocks to check end-to-end delay, recording retries, packet loss and the longest continuous interruption.',
'先檢查序號與時間戳，避免把重播封包誤認為狀態恢復。~Check sequence numbers and timestamps before interpreting a replayed packet as state recovery.')
d('interlock','布林組合數表示測試狀態空間的大小，並不代表每個狀態在現場都可達或安全。應把占用、道岔鎖閉和授權的邏輯關係明列，逐項證明危險組合會被拒絕。~The Boolean count describes the size of a test state space, not that every state is reachable or safe in service. Explicitly state relations among occupation, point locking and authority, and demonstrate that hazardous combinations are rejected.',
'從真值表逐列執行故障注入，記錄預期拒絕與實際輸出，並覆核非法狀態不可授權。~Execute fault injection row by row from the truth table, recording expected refusal and actual output, and verify that illegal states receive no authority.',
'狀態覆蓋率高仍可能缺少危險轉移，須查事件先後。~High state coverage can still miss a hazardous transition; inspect event ordering as well.')
d('brakecurve','目標速度不一定是零，進入較低速區也需要保護距離。計算使用同一距離基準與速度單位，並把定位誤差和延遲裕度分開，才能避免重複或漏加安全邊界。~The target speed need not be zero: entry into a lower-speed section also requires protection distance. Use one distance reference and consistent speed units. Keep localisation uncertainty and delay margins separate to prevent duplicated or omitted boundaries.',
'以已知初速與目標速度重播控制資料，核對速度單位、里程方向及列車前端參考位置。~Replay control data at known initial and target speeds, checking speed units, chainage direction and the reference position of the train front.',
'若目標速度高於初速，此減速模型的工況設定便不成立。~If target speed exceeds initial speed, the stated deceleration case no longer applies.')
d('axle','動態放大係數只是一種教學集中描述，不能代替接觸衝擊的頻譜。軸重分配、輪徑及軌道不平順會讓不同車輪荷重不同，應保留空車與滿載情境。~A dynamic amplification factor is a compact teaching representation, not a replacement for an impact spectrum. Axle distribution, wheel diameter and track irregularity can produce different wheel loads; retain both empty and loaded conditions.',
'在已知靜態軸重下校正量測，核對左右輪荷重總和，並比較不同速度的峰值。~Calibrate against known static axle load, check the sum of left and right wheel loads, and compare peaks at different speeds.',
'單一輪峰值不能直接當作整列平均軸重，須查荷重分配。~One wheel-load peak cannot represent the train’s mean axle load; inspect load distribution.')
d('fatigue','線性累積損傷不保留載重順序，也不能自行描述腐蝕、裂紋閉合和超載效應。疲勞曲線的適用材料與應力定義必須一致，否則算出的壽命比例沒有可比性。~Linear cumulative damage does not retain load order and cannot independently describe corrosion, crack closure or overload effects. The fatigue curve must match the material and stress definition; otherwise calculated life fractions are not comparable.',
'從原始應變檢查應力換算與循環計數，核對各級距的次數總和及疲勞曲線來源。~Check stress conversion and cycle counting from raw strain, verifying total counts across bins and the source of the fatigue curve.',
'若應力級距漏計，累積損傷偏低不能證明構件仍完好。~Understated damage caused by omitted stress bins is not evidence that the component remains sound.')
d('snow','融雪至少要提供冰融化所需潛熱；若初溫低於冰點，還須先加熱到融點。此式僅算宣告的能量項，不能把理想加熱功率直接當成現場融雪產能。~Melting requires latent heat; snow initially below freezing must first be heated to the melting point. This expression includes only declared energy terms, so ideal heater power cannot be equated directly with field snow-removal capacity.',
'先稱量積雪並量測初溫，核對加熱時間與電量，另記融水、散熱及持續降雪。~Weigh the snow and measure its initial temperature, verify heating time and electricity, and separately record meltwater, heat loss and continuing snowfall.',
'新增降雪和散熱未計入時，融雪速度必然偏向理想值。~Omitting new snowfall and heat loss biases the melting-rate estimate toward ideal conditions.')
d('crosswind','橫向力依側風分量平方變化，列車姿態和地形會改變受風面積及係數。此力尺度不直接給出傾覆門檻；還需重心、輪重減載、懸吊和陣風時間歷程。~Lateral force varies with squared crosswind component, while vehicle attitude and terrain change exposed area and coefficients. The force scale does not directly yield an overturning threshold; centre of gravity, wheel unloading, suspension and gust history remain necessary.',
'核對風速計高度與方向，保存陣風時序，將列車姿態與側向加速度放在同一時間軸。~Verify anemometer height and orientation, retain gust histories, and align vehicle attitude with lateral acceleration on one timeline.',
'日平均風速會掩蓋陣風，需檢查量測平均時間與峰值。~Daily mean wind hides gusts; inspect averaging duration and the recorded peaks.')
d('noise','分貝是對數量，聲源互不相干時應先轉回線性能量再相加。頻率加權和量測時間必須相同，否則兩個數字不能直接合成；有相干干涉時還需相位資訊。~Decibels are logarithmic, so incoherent sources must be converted to linear energy before summation. Frequency weighting and observation duration must match. Coherent interference additionally requires phase information and is not captured by the energy-sum model.',
'以聲級校正器檢查儀器前後漂移，記錄頻率加權和平均時間，再測背景聲單獨量級。~Check instrument drift with a sound calibrator before and after measurement, record frequency weighting and averaging time, and measure background separately.',
'若背景聲未扣除，不能把全部合成量歸因於列車。~Without separate background measurement, the complete combined level cannot be attributed to the train.')
d('drain','合理化流量法假定雨強與集流條件相符，面積及逕流係數也須明確。它估算峰值流率而非完整洪水歷線；抽水或蓄水設計還需對時間積分和出口條件。~The rational estimate assumes rainfall intensity compatible with catchment response and explicit area and runoff coefficient. It gives a peak rate, not a complete hydrograph. Pumping or storage design additionally requires time integration and outlet conditions.',
'核對雨量單位和有效集水邊界，量測泵浦出流與集水井水位變化，以體積守恆互證。~Verify rainfall units and catchment boundaries, measure pump outflow and sump-level change, and cross-check them through volume conservation.',
'排水堵塞改變有效出流，不能只用較大泵浦銘牌值補償。~Blocked drainage changes effective outflow and cannot be compensated merely by a larger pump nameplate rating.')
d('freeze','凍結深度對時間的平方根敏感度來自移動相界面熱量平衡。均質導熱與固定邊界是強假設，地下水對流、含冰量改變和日夜循環都可能使相界面偏離此結果。~Square-root time dependence of freezing depth arises from the moving-boundary heat balance. Homogeneous conduction and a fixed boundary are strong assumptions; groundwater advection, changing ice content and daily thermal cycles can shift the interface away from this estimate.',
'用不同深度溫度鏈定位零度附近相界面，檢查土壤含水率與表面熱邊界的變化。~Use temperature strings at several depths to locate the near-freezing interface, and check changes in soil moisture and surface thermal boundary.',
'溫度接近零度不代表凍結比例固定，須核對潛熱與含水量。~Near-zero temperature does not imply a fixed frozen fraction; inspect latent heat and water content.')
d('cooling','顯熱負載決定溫度改變需求，但高濕環境還有潛熱除濕與新風處理。冷卻量和耗電量也不同，兩者需要效率或性能係數連結，不能把熱量數字當作電表讀值。~Sensible load describes temperature-related demand, while humidity introduces latent dehumidification and outdoor-air treatment. Cooling delivered and electricity consumed are different quantities, connected through efficiency or a performance coefficient rather than treated as identical meter readings.',
'同步量測進出風溫度、流量和耗電，另記濕度與新風比例，確認顯熱邊界一致。~Measure inlet and outlet air temperature, airflow and electricity together, separately recording humidity and outdoor-air fraction to confirm consistent sensible boundaries.',
'濕度升高仍可能需要更多冷量，即使乾球溫度沒有改變。~Rising humidity can require more cooling even if the dry-bulb temperature has not changed.')
d('filter','濾材阻力係數描述既定流動條件下的壓力損失，積塵會改變係數也可能降低風量。只看壓差下降可能誤判濾材變乾淨，實際上可能是風機降速或風道旁通。~The filter coefficient describes pressure loss under specified flow conditions. Dust changes that coefficient and may reduce flow. Falling pressure drop can misleadingly suggest a cleaner filter when the cause is fan slowdown or duct bypass.',
'檢查壓差取壓點位置與零點，同步記錄風量、風機轉速和濾材累積質量。~Verify differential-pressure tap locations and zero, recording airflow, fan speed and accumulated filter mass at the same time.',
'壓差很低也可能是旁通，須核對濾材密封及實際風量。~Very low pressure drop can indicate bypass; check filter sealing and actual airflow.')
d('platform','密度是人數除以有效面積，不直接描述人群流速或推擠力。設備、柱子及候車線會減少可用空間；安全通道應另列，不能為了降低平均密度而計入不可占用區域。~Density divides occupancy by usable area but does not directly describe walking speed or crowd pressure. Equipment, columns and waiting boundaries reduce usable space. Reserved circulation must be accounted separately, not included merely to lower the reported average density.',
'以分區影片計數核對總人數，量測淨面積，並同時記錄局部瓶頸及進出流量。~Cross-check total occupancy with zonal video counts, measure net area, and record local bottlenecks and entry-exit flows simultaneously.',
'總平均密度低仍可能局部壅塞，須查看門口與樓梯區域。~Low overall mean density can coexist with local crowding; inspect doorway and stair zones.')
d('escalator','階梯間距與速度決定理論階梯通過率，每階占用率則把機械運動轉成載客量。旅客猶豫、行李及出口壅塞會降低實際通過率，不能以理論值直接證明疏散能力。~Step pitch and speed determine theoretical step passage, while occupancy per step converts mechanical motion into passenger flow. Hesitation, luggage and blocked exits reduce delivery, so the theoretical rate cannot directly demonstrate evacuation capacity.',
'核對階梯間距與帶速，以入口及出口計數比較乘客流量，另記停頓和空階比例。~Verify step pitch and belt speed, compare entry and exit passenger counts, and separately record stoppages and empty-step proportions.',
'出口堵塞時提高帶速可能加劇累積，需先檢查出口容量。~Increasing belt speed can worsen accumulation at a blocked outlet; inspect outlet capacity first.')
d('doors','單門關閉成功率與全列全部必要門組確認的機率不同。獨立假設只供算例；共用電源、控制訊息或旅客行為可能造成相關失效，實務上須記錄每扇門與整列狀態。~One door’s closure success differs from the probability that all required doors confirm. Independence is only an exercise assumption: shared power, control messages or passenger behaviour can cause correlated failure. Record individual and whole-train states in practice.',
'對每扇門同步記錄開關命令、位置與鎖閉確認，核對重試次數及共用控制事件。~Record command, position and lock confirmation synchronously for every door, checking retries and events in the shared controller.',
'多門同時異常需先查共用控制，不能直接當成獨立故障。~Simultaneous door anomalies require checking shared control before classifying them as independent failures.')
d('ventilation','換氣率把流量與空間容積連結，但平均換氣不保證每個角落都被掃流。短路流、漏風和污染源位置會改變稀釋效果，應以流量和示蹤濃度共同檢查混合假設。~Air-change rate links flow to room volume, but an average does not ensure every corner is swept. Short-circuit flow, leakage and source location alter dilution. Check the mixing assumption with both airflow and tracer-concentration measurements.',
'校正風量計並做多點斷面積分，以示蹤衰減或濃度分布核對混合，保留門開關狀態。~Calibrate airflow instruments and integrate a multipoint section, then check mixing with tracer decay or concentration distribution while retaining door states.',
'風機有轉不代表有效換氣，需查風道旁通和氣流短路。~A running fan does not prove effective ventilation; inspect duct bypass and airflow short-circuiting.')
d('piston','列車排開體積的模型首先遵守連續方程，但洩漏、車站開口與可壓縮效應會改變實際流場。應明確使用剩餘通流面積，不能用整個隧道面積忽略車體阻塞。~A displaced-volume model first follows continuity, but leakage, station openings and compressibility alter the actual field. Use the remaining flow area explicitly rather than the whole tunnel area while ignoring train blockage.',
'在列車通過前後同步量測風速、壓力及位置，以多點截面平均避免局部噴流誤差。~Synchronise airflow, pressure and train position around passage, using a multipoint section average to avoid bias from local jets.',
'局部風速尖峰不能當作整段平均流量，須核對截面分布。~A local velocity peak cannot represent whole-section flow; inspect the cross-sectional distribution.')
d('queue','利用率接近一時，平均等候對微小需求變化極敏感。此封閉式結果依賴隨機到達與服務分布及穩態假設；飛機或活動散場的批次到達應另用事件模擬。~As utilisation approaches unity, mean waiting becomes highly sensitive to demand. The closed-form result relies on arrival, service-distribution and steady-state assumptions. Flight arrivals or event-release batches require a separate event simulation.',
'記錄逐人到達、開始服務及離開時刻，以事件重播核對等候分布並檢查是否穩態。~Record each arrival, service start and departure, then replay events to check the waiting-time distribution and whether a steady state exists.',
'若到達率不小於服務率，穩態等候公式便不可使用。~If arrival rate is not below service rate, the steady-state waiting formula is inapplicable.')
d('availability','平均故障間隔和平均修復時間必須使用相同服務邊界；備件等待與到場時間若被排除，數字就不能描述旅客看到的中斷。短期樣本也應報告事件數與觀測時間。~Mean time between failures and mean repair time require a common service boundary. Excluding spare-part waiting or travel time prevents the figure from describing passenger-visible interruption. Short samples should also report event count and observation duration.',
'逐項對照故障開始、服務恢復與維修完成時間，公開排除項，並核對總觀測時數。~Cross-check fault start, service restoration and repair completion for each event, disclose exclusions, and verify total observed hours.',
'修好設備和恢復服務可能不同時，須分別記錄終點。~Equipment repair and service restoration may occur at different times; record both endpoints.')
d('rubber','平均接觸壓力只反映總輪載除以有效面積，不能描述胎面局部剪應力。充氣狀態、溫度與導向作用會改變接觸形狀；輪胎承載與側向導向必須分開建模。~Mean contact pressure only divides total wheel load by effective area and does not describe local tread shear. Inflation, temperature and guidance alter the contact shape. Vertical tyre support and lateral guidance must be modelled separately.',
'以壓力感測膜或校正平台核對接觸區，量測輪載和胎壓，並保留溫度條件。~Check the contact region with pressure film or a calibrated platform, measure wheel load and inflation pressure, and retain temperature conditions.',
'胎面局部壓力可能高於平均值，須查看接觸面分布。~Local tread pressure can exceed the mean; inspect its distribution over the contact patch.')
d('baggage','單件服務時間決定理論處理率，但旅客會以群組攜帶不同件數到達。服務台之間的分流、行李安放和下游輸送都可能改變實際瓶頸，應逐事件保留記錄。~Individual handling time determines a theoretical rate, but groups arrive with different numbers of items. Counter allocation, baggage placement and downstream transport can move the actual bottleneck, so retain event-by-event records.',
'分別記錄每位旅客件數、服務開始和完成時間，核對下游暫存是否造成櫃台停等。~Record item count, service start and completion for each passenger, checking whether downstream storage forces the counter to pause.',
'處理台空閒不代表無瓶頸，可能是下游行李區已滿。~An idle counter does not prove spare capacity; downstream baggage storage may already be full.')
d('mixed','追趕時間取決於起始間隔和兩列相對速度，不能只看快車速度。若兩列會停站或受訊號限制，速度必須改成分段函數，並把進路占用放回事件圖。~Catch-up time depends on starting separation and relative speed, not only the faster train’s speed. If either train stops or encounters signalling constraints, use piecewise speed functions and restore route occupation to the event diagram.',
'以逐站到發時刻重建距離時間圖，核對起始間隔和各段速度，並標示待避占用。~Rebuild a distance-time diagram from station arrivals and departures, verifying initial separation and segment speeds and marking passing occupation.',
'快慢車速度相同時不能用追趕公式分母，須重設工況。~Equal train speeds invalidate the catch-up denominator; redefine the operating case.')
d('neutral','無牽引不等於無運動，列車以動能克服所宣告的阻力。若距離超過此阻力下的可滑行距離，平方根將無實數解，表示通過情境不成立而非計算器錯誤。~No traction does not mean no motion: kinetic energy overcomes the declared resistance. If the section exceeds the available coasting distance, the square root has no real solution, indicating an infeasible passage case rather than a calculator malfunction.',
'以入口和出口獨立速度對照滑行距離，核對斷電區時間戳及坡度是否被模型排除。~Compare independently measured entry and exit speeds with coasting distance, checking power-off timestamps and whether gradient is excluded.',
'若計算顯示無法通過，不能把負根號截成零後繼續排程。~If passage is infeasible, do not clamp a negative radicand to zero and continue scheduling.')
d('sampling','取樣頻率超過訊號最高頻率兩倍是重建的必要起點，仍需要抗混疊濾波及足夠振幅精度。尖峰與非平穩事件的要求不同，應從量測目的回推頻寬與記錄長度。~Sampling above twice the highest signal frequency is a starting condition for reconstruction, but anti-alias filtering and amplitude accuracy remain necessary. Peaks and nonstationary events have different needs; derive bandwidth and recording duration from the measurement objective.',
'用已知頻率訊號測試整條量測鏈，檢查抗混疊濾波器、時鐘誤差與遺漏樣本。~Test the complete measurement chain with a known-frequency signal, checking anti-alias filtering, clock error and missing samples.',
'降低取樣率後出現新低頻峰值，應先查混疊而非機械故障。~A new low-frequency peak after downsampling requires checking aliasing before diagnosing a mechanical fault.')
d('bearing','幾何故障頻率是理想滾動關係，實際滑移會移動頻率或展寬峰值。量測頻譜需和當時轉速一起解讀，不能把固定頻率峰直接指派給某個故障部位。~Geometric defect frequencies assume ideal rolling; slip can shift or broaden peaks. Interpret the measured spectrum together with contemporaneous rotation speed instead of assigning a fixed peak directly to a defect location.',
'以獨立轉速計核對每段資料，保留頻譜解析度和窗函數，並比較不同轉速的階次。~Verify each data segment with an independent tachometer, retain spectral resolution and window function, and compare orders across rotation speeds.',
'速度改變後峰值若不隨階次移動，須檢查其他激振來源。~If a peak does not track rotational order as speed changes, inspect other excitation sources.')
d('fleet','循環時間除以班距後必須向上取整，半列車不能提供完整班次。此數量是投入循環的最低值，維修備用、延誤緩衝與不同分支運轉仍需額外配置。~Divide cycle time by headway and round upward because a fraction of a train cannot provide a full departure. This is the minimum circulating requirement; maintenance spares, delay buffers and branch-specific operation need additional allocation.',
'核對往返與折返時間使用同一單位，以逐列時刻表重播，檢查每次發車是否有車可用。~Verify consistent units for round-trip and turnaround times, replay a train-by-train timetable, and check vehicle availability at every departure.',
'循環時間稍增可能跨過整數門檻，不能只比較百分比。~A small cycle-time increase can cross an integer fleet threshold; percentages alone are insufficient.')
d('backup','可用電量應扣除允許放電深度與轉換損失，負載也可能隨時間變化。銘牌容量的測試溫度和放電倍率會影響實際結果，續航計算不能取代受控放電驗證。~Usable energy must account for permitted discharge depth and conversion losses, while load may vary over time. Test temperature and discharge rate influence rated capacity, so an endurance calculation cannot replace controlled discharge verification.',
'以受控負載記錄電池電壓、電流與溫度，積分可用電量，核對低壓切斷時刻。~Record battery voltage, current and temperature under controlled load, integrate usable energy, and verify the low-voltage cut-off time.',
'電池電壓正常不代表容量足夠，需檢查負載下放電曲線。~Normal open-circuit voltage does not prove sufficient capacity; inspect the loaded discharge curve.')
d('redundancy','獨立失效機率相乘只在共同原因可忽略時成立。共用機房、電源、時鐘或軟體缺陷會使冗餘失去預期效果；應把獨立事件與共同事件分成不同邏輯項。~Multiplying failure probabilities requires negligible common causes. Shared rooms, power, clocks or software defects can defeat expected redundancy. Represent independent events and common events as separate logical terms rather than silently combining them.',
'列出兩通道共用的實體與軟體資源，分開注入單路故障及共因故障，核對失效狀態。~List physical and software resources shared by both channels, inject individual and common-cause faults separately, and verify resulting failure states.',
'兩個盒子不等於兩個獨立通道，須核對共用依賴。~Two boxes do not imply two independent channels; inspect their shared dependencies.')
d('pressure','溫度必須使用絕對溫標，且壓力必須是絕對壓力。固定體積與固定氣體質量的假設排除了漏氣和主動調壓，因此這個模型只能用來檢查封閉容積的基本尺度。~Temperature must use an absolute scale and pressure must be absolute. Fixed volume and gas mass exclude leakage and active regulation, so this model only checks the basic scale of behaviour in a sealed volume.',
'校正壓力零點並換算表壓與絕對壓力，量測容積與氣體溫度，檢查漏氣證據。~Calibrate pressure zero and distinguish gauge from absolute pressure, measure volume and gas temperature, and inspect evidence of leakage.',
'若使用攝氏溫度直接作比例，結果沒有正確熱力學意義。~Ratios formed directly from Celsius temperature have no correct thermodynamic interpretation here.')
d('sand','濃度乘風量得到進入設備的質量率，捕集效率再決定留在濾材的比例。粒徑分布與濾材負載會改變效率；因此算例的固定值只是可重算基準，並非所有砂塵條件通用。~Concentration times airflow gives incoming mass rate, and collection efficiency determines retained mass. Particle sizes and filter loading change efficiency. A fixed efficiency is therefore a reproducible baseline, not a universal value for every dusty condition.',
'以進出氣濃度和濾材前後稱重互證，保留粒徑範圍、風量及取樣時間。~Cross-check inlet-outlet concentration against filter mass change, retaining particle-size range, airflow and sampling duration.',
'濾材破損時壓差可能下降而穿透增加，須同查出氣濃度。~A torn filter may show lower pressure drop and greater penetration; check outlet concentration too.')
d('survey','獨立量測誤差的平方和開根號只適用於無相關偏差的情境。儀器零點或共同基準誤差不會隨測次增加自動消失；閉合差能揭露不一致，卻不能單獨證明基點穩定。~Root-sum-square uncertainty requires independent errors without shared bias. Instrument zero or a common datum error does not disappear with more observations. Closure can reveal inconsistency but cannot alone prove that the reference point is stable.',
'以反向觀測、閉合路線和外部基準交叉檢核，分開報告隨機標準差與可疑系統偏差。~Cross-check reversed observations, closed loops and external references, reporting random standard deviation separately from suspected systematic bias.',
'閉合良好仍可能全部同向漂移，須使用外部穩定基準。~Good closure can coexist with common drift; an external stable reference remains necessary.')
d('grout','環隙體積由外內斷面差乘長度得到，內外直徑不可對調。超灌係數只是體積預算，不能推論地層已被完全填滿；實注壓力、回流與沉陷反應仍需驗證。~Annular volume is the difference between outer and inner areas multiplied by length; diameters must not be reversed. An excess factor is only a volume allowance, not proof of complete filling. Injection pressure, returns and settlement response still require verification.',
'校對泵送流量計與漿液批次密度，分開累計注入、回流及廢棄量，核對幾何尺寸。~Calibrate pump flow and batch density, separately total injection, return and waste volumes, and verify geometric dimensions.',
'達到預算漿量不等於填滿環隙，須查回流和漏失。~Reaching the budgeted grout volume does not prove annulus filling; inspect returns and losses.')
d('transfer','距離除速度只表示行走或移動時間，等待列車、排隊和辨識路徑應另列。使用單一平均速度會掩蓋行李、行動能力和雙向干擾，應以分段分群資料檢查。~Distance divided by speed represents movement only; train waiting, queueing and wayfinding need separate terms. One mean speed hides baggage, mobility differences and opposing flow. Check the result with segmented measurements for relevant passenger groups.',
'在路徑起終點對時，逐段記錄水平、垂直與等待時間，核對是否漏計驗票或排隊。~Synchronise route endpoints, record horizontal movement, vertical movement and waiting separately, and check for omitted gate processing or queues.',
'旅客走錯路會改變實際距離，需比較引導前後的路徑。~Wrong turns change actual distance; compare observed routes before and after guidance changes.')
d('congestion','流率是密度乘速度再乘通道寬度，增加密度也可能降低速度。簡化線性關係只用來說明最佳流率位置，不代表現場人群一定遵循同一堵塞密度或行為。~Flow is density times speed times width, and greater density can reduce speed. A linear relation illustrates the location of peak flow, not that real crowds share one jam density or behavioural response.',
'以固定觀測區同步計數密度與通過流率，量測有效淨寬，檢查雙向流及停留者。~Measure density and passing flow simultaneously in a fixed observation zone, verify clear width, and identify opposing flows and stationary occupants.',
'平均速度下降可能來自停留而非擁擠，須查看個別軌跡。~Lower mean speed may reflect intentional stopping rather than crowding; inspect individual trajectories.')
d('clearance','剩餘淨空須扣除車體動態位移與施工偏差，不能只比較名目寬度。各誤差可能同向或相關，最不利組合與統計組合必須明確區分，不能任意混用。~Remaining clearance must account for vehicle movement and construction tolerance, not only nominal width. Errors can align or correlate, so worst-case and statistical combinations must be explicitly distinguished rather than mixed without justification.',
'以校正掃描量測固定障礙，核對車體參考座標及動態位移包絡，保留最小距離位置。~Measure fixed obstacles with calibrated scanning, verify vehicle reference coordinates and dynamic envelopes, and retain the location of minimum separation.',
'最小淨空位置可能在曲線偏移處，不能只量直線斷面。~Minimum clearance may occur at curve offsets, so measurements of straight sections alone are insufficient.')
d('construction','可施工時間等於總窗口扣掉保護設置、測試及還路等必要活動。這些活動可能有不可重疊的安全依賴；趕工不能直接刪除，應以資源和先後順序改變排程。~Usable work time equals the possession window minus protection, testing and handback activities. These can have nonoverlapping safety dependencies and cannot simply be deleted to accelerate work. Change scheduling through resources and legitimate task order.',
'逐項記錄窗口開始、保護完成、施工完成與還路時刻，核對前置條件及實際資源。~Log possession start, protection completion, work completion and handback times, checking mandatory prerequisites and resources actually available.',
'施工完成不等於可還路，需保留檢查測試與解除保護時間。~Work completion is not readiness for handback; retain inspection, testing and protection-removal time.')
# Numeric-model reconciliation: these paragraphs deliberately track the actual formula.
d('tunnelwave','波傳時間由傳播距離除以聲速決定，與列車走完整段的時間不同。此式只預測到達時序而不預測波幅；洞口形狀、列車頭型和反射決定的壓力變化須用其他流動模型。~Wave travel time is propagation distance divided by sound speed, not the time for the train to traverse the section. This expression predicts arrival timing, not amplitude. Portal geometry, train-nose shape and reflections require additional flow models to predict pressure changes.',
'在洞口與洞內配置同步壓力測點，對照列車頭部通過時刻，分辨首波與後續反射。~Synchronise pressure sensors at the portal and inside the tunnel with nose-passage time, distinguishing the first wave from later reflections.',
'單點峰值不足以判別首波，須檢查測點間傳遞時差。~A single peak cannot identify the first wave; inspect propagation delay between sensors.')
d('isolation','此式描述單自由度線性隔振系統的力傳遞率，頻率比是激振頻率除以固有頻率。增加阻尼有助於抑制共振，但在高頻隔振區不一定降低傳遞；必須先辨認工況所在區域。~This expression describes force transmissibility of a linear single-degree-of-freedom isolator. Frequency ratio is excitation frequency divided by natural frequency. Added damping suppresses resonance but need not reduce transmission in the high-frequency isolation region, so identify the operating region first.',
'同步量測基座與支承反力頻譜，核對激振頻率、固有頻率和阻尼，檢查兩測點相位。~Measure base and transmitted-force spectra synchronously, verifying excitation frequency, natural frequency and damping while checking phase between measurement points.',
'阻尼器劣化與剛度改變會有不同頻譜，須分開辨識。~Damper deterioration and stiffness change produce different spectral effects and must be identified separately.')
d('localize','兩個獨立無偏估計的資訊量可以相加，較小變異數應獲較大權重。共同偏差不會被這種融合消除，相關性也會破壞公式；較小標準差只能表示宣告模型下的精密度。~Information from two independent unbiased estimates can be combined, assigning greater weight to smaller variance. Shared bias is not removed by this fusion, and correlation invalidates the expression. Smaller standard deviation represents precision only under the declared statistical model.',
'以外部參考位置核對兩感測器殘差，檢查平均偏差及相關係數，再比較融合後覆蓋範圍。~Check both sensor residuals against an external position reference, examine mean bias and correlation, and compare coverage after fusion.',
'若兩感測器共用錯誤基準，融合後仍會保持共同偏差。~If both sensors share a wrong reference, the fused result retains the common bias.')
d('axle','此式把輪力分配到假想均勻接觸面積，只能給平均壓力。實際輪軌接觸可能呈非均勻橢圓壓力分布，最大值還受曲率、材料與接觸狀態影響，不能直接由平均值驗收。~The expression distributes wheel force over a hypothetical uniform contact area and gives mean pressure only. Real wheel-rail contact can have a nonuniform elliptical pressure distribution. Peak pressure also depends on curvature, material and contact state and cannot be accepted from the mean alone.',
'以校正輪力和接觸斑量測核對平均壓力，另列接觸邊緣與中心差異及有效面積誤差。~Check mean pressure using calibrated wheel force and contact-patch measurements, separately recording edge-centre differences and effective-area uncertainty.',
'局部峰值可能高於平均壓力，須檢查接觸形狀與材料反應。~Local peaks can exceed mean pressure; inspect contact shape and material response.')
d('freeze','熱量除以單位體積融冰潛熱給出等效融化深度，模型只做能量帳。它沒有求解隨時間移動的凍融前緣，也未計土體顯熱、地下水輸熱與表面散熱，因此不能直接預測凍土壽命。~Heat divided by latent melting energy per unit volume gives an equivalent thaw depth. This is an energy account, not a solution for a time-dependent thaw front. Soil sensible heat, groundwater transport and surface losses remain excluded, so it cannot directly predict permafrost life.',
'用不同深度溫度鏈與土壤含冰量取樣核對輸入，另以實測融深檢查能量帳缺少的項目。~Check inputs using temperature strings and ice-content samples, then compare measured thaw depth to identify terms absent from the energy account.',
'冰量分率錯估會直接改變融深，須查取樣空間代表性。~An incorrect ice fraction directly changes thaw depth; inspect the spatial representativeness of samples.')
d('filter','風機功率等於壓力差乘體積流率再除以宣告效率，壓力與流量必須使用同一工作點。積塵使阻力和風機工作點共同改變，固定流量算例不能預測未控制風量時的耗電。~Fan power equals pressure difference times volume flow divided by the declared efficiency. Pressure and flow must refer to one operating point. Dust changes resistance and the fan operating point together, so a fixed-flow example cannot predict consumption without airflow control.',
'校正取壓點與風量計，同步量測電功率，核對效率是否包含馬達與驅動器損失。~Calibrate pressure taps and airflow measurement, record electric power simultaneously, and check whether efficiency includes motor and drive losses.',
'壓差很低也可能是旁通，須核對濾材密封及實際風量。~Very low pressure drop can indicate bypass; check filter sealing and actual airflow.')
d('doors','停車、測量與門位置三個獨立零均值誤差以變異數相加，再取平方根得到合成標準差。這不是最大偏移保證，也不含共同系統偏差；機械淨空及容許對位範圍須另外核對。~Three independent zero-mean errors in stopping, surveying and door position combine through summed variances. The square root gives a standard deviation, not a guaranteed maximum offset. Shared bias is excluded, and mechanical clearance and permitted alignment ranges require separate checks.',
'以獨立基準重複量測停準與門位，檢查各誤差平均值、相關性和單位，再核對合成分布。~Repeat stopping and door-position measurements against an independent reference, check each mean, correlation and unit, and compare the combined distribution.',
'若共同定位偏差存在，平方和模型會低估實際對位偏移。~A shared positioning bias makes the root-sum-square model understate actual alignment offset.')
d('ventilation','完全混合且污染源已停止時，濃度以指數衰減；剩餘比例必須介於零與一。換氣率是流量除以容積，清除時間還依目標濃度而變，不能把一次換氣直接當成全部清除。~For perfect mixing after the source stops, concentration decays exponentially and the remaining fraction lies between zero and one. Air-change rate is flow divided by volume, while clearance time also depends on target concentration. One air change does not mean complete removal.',
'以安全示蹤氣體衰減核對時間常數，多點量測濃度並保留門狀態，檢查是否存在未停止源。~Check the time constant with safe tracer decay, measure concentration at multiple points, retain door states, and check for a continuing source.',
'風機有轉不代表有效稀釋，需查風道旁通和持續污染源。~A running fan does not prove effective dilution; inspect bypass and continuing contaminant sources.')
d('queue','隨機到站旅客更容易遇到較長班距，因為長區間占較多時間，因此平均等候與班距變異數有關。公式假定旅客到達獨立於班表且每班可上車，不能表示服務櫃台或容量不足的隊列。~Random arrivals encounter longer headways more often because those intervals occupy more time. Mean waiting therefore depends on headway variance. The formula assumes arrivals independent of the timetable and successful boarding on every train; it does not model counters or capacity-constrained queues.',
'從逐列到站時間重建班距平均與標準差，將旅客隨機到達事件重播，核對等候樣本平均。~Reconstruct mean and standard deviation from successive train arrivals, replay random passenger arrivals, and compare the sampled mean waiting time.',
'若滿載造成無法上車，需額外追蹤留下隊列而不能沿用公式。~When full trains prevent boarding, track the remaining queue separately instead of reusing this formula.')
d('rubber','滾動阻力係數乘法向荷重得到阻力，再乘速度才是功率。輪胎壓力、溫度與變形影響係數；此模型沒有計入導向輪、風阻與加速能量，不能代表整車總耗電。~Rolling-resistance coefficient times normal load gives force, and multiplying by speed gives power. Tyre inflation, temperature and deformation influence the coefficient. Guidance wheels, aerodynamic drag and acceleration are excluded, so this does not represent total vehicle electricity.',
'在已知輪載與穩定速度下量測牽引力，記錄胎壓及溫度，扣除可辨識的其他阻力。~Measure tractive force at known normal load and steady speed, record tyre pressure and temperature, and remove identifiable other resistance.',
'胎壓下降可能提高滾阻，需以同速同載量測判別變化。~Lower inflation can raise rolling resistance; compare measurements at equal speed and load.')
d('baggage','等效需求把攜行李旅客依宣告係數換算為普通旅客負荷，不是把人數真的增加。係數需對應車門交換、通道占用等指定用途，不能拿一個值同時代表所有服務時間。~Equivalent demand converts baggage travellers into ordinary-passenger load using a declared factor; it does not create additional people. The factor must correspond to a specified purpose such as door exchange or space occupation, not represent all service times simultaneously.',
'分別計數一般旅客與行李旅客，以實測交換時間或占用面積校準係數，保留用途與區間。~Count ordinary and baggage passengers separately, calibrate the factor against exchange time or occupied area, and retain its purpose and range.',
'相同人數可能有不同負荷，需保留行李比例而非只報總人數。~Equal headcounts can impose different loads; retain baggage proportions rather than reporting total people only.')
d('pressure','此理想氣體式以絕對壓力和絕對溫度估算空氣密度，壓力不代表氧氣比例。高原環境的密度可影響氣動和冷卻估算，但人員生理與主動加壓系統需要另外分析。~This ideal-gas expression estimates air density from absolute pressure and temperature; pressure is not an oxygen fraction. Altitude-dependent density can affect aerodynamic and cooling estimates, while human physiology and active pressurisation require separate analysis.',
'校正絕對壓力計並量測同位置氣溫，核對溫標換算，必要時另列濕度造成的氣體性質差異。~Calibrate the absolute-pressure sensor and measure temperature at the same location, checking the temperature conversion and separately considering humidity effects.',
'若使用攝氏溫度直接作分母，空氣密度會失去正確物理意義。~Using Celsius temperature directly in the denominator produces a physically incorrect air density.')
d('sand','沉積通量乘接收面積與時間得到積砂質量，通量已是單位面積的到達率。它不同於空氣中的濃度；要從濃度推回沉積，還需風速、粒徑及捕集機制。~Deposition flux times receiving area and time gives accumulated sand mass. Flux is already an arrival rate per unit area and differs from airborne concentration. Deriving deposition from concentration also requires wind, particle size and a capture mechanism.',
'用已知面積收集盤在指定時間稱重，保留風向與取樣位置，並檢查再懸浮和散失。~Weigh collection trays of known area over a stated interval, retain wind direction and sampling location, and inspect resuspension and losses.',
'平均沉積通量可能漏掉局部堆砂，須比較不同設備位置。~Mean deposition flux can hide local drifts; compare different equipment locations.')
d('survey','兩座標差的歐氏長度表示平面殘差大小，不是隨機標準差。先把兩套座標轉到相同基準和單位，再檢查各方向偏差；共同平移可能讓相對殘差很小但絕對位置仍錯。~The Euclidean length of two coordinate differences measures planar residual, not random standard deviation. Transform both coordinate sets to one datum and unit before inspecting directional differences. Common translation can leave a small relative residual while absolute position remains wrong.',
'以反向觀測、閉合路線和外部基準交叉檢核，分開報告平面殘差與可疑共同偏差。~Cross-check reversed observations, closed loops and external references, reporting planar residual separately from suspected shared bias.',
'閉合良好仍可能全部同向漂移，須使用外部穩定基準。~Good closure can coexist with common drift; an external stable reference remains necessary.')
d('grout','此算例把空隙視為長乘寬乘均勻厚度的薄層，再乘假定餘量。它不是完整圓環幾何；若用於環隙局部展開，須說明薄層近似，且不能由注入總量推論填充均勻。~This example treats a void as length times width times uniform thickness with an assumed allowance. It is not full annular geometry. A locally unwrapped annulus requires an explicit thin-layer approximation, and total injection does not establish uniform filling.',
'校對泵送流量計與漿液批次密度，分開累計注入、回流及廢棄量，核對薄層幾何尺寸。~Calibrate pump flow and batch density, separately total injection, return and waste volumes, and verify the thin-layer dimensions.',
'達到預算漿量不等於填滿空隙，須查回流和漏失。~Reaching the budgeted grout volume does not prove void filling; inspect returns and losses.')
d('congestion','容量減去兩支流給出平均服務餘裕，負值表示隊列會累積而非負人數。此代數式不描述人群密度與速度的關係；要算實際隊列長度，必須把淨流量隨時間積分。~Capacity minus two incoming streams gives mean service margin; a negative value indicates accumulating queues, not negative people. This algebra does not describe the density-speed relationship. Physical queue length requires integrating net flow over time.',
'同步量測兩入口與出口流量，採相同時間窗並以人數守恆核對區域內隊列的增減。~Measure both inlet flows and outlet flow synchronously, use identical time windows, and check queue changes through conservation of people.',
'平均餘裕為正仍可能短時超載，須核對脈衝到達。~Positive mean margin can coexist with short overloads; inspect pulsed arrivals.')
